<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seneca Lake</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seneca Lake is the largest of the Finger Lakes of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, about 60 km long and over 180 m deep. It lay at the eastern edge of the Seneca <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>, which stretched west to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genesee-river">Genesee River</a>. The lake is now known for its vineyards and wineries.</p></div>
